The image should feel generous and prominent without occupying an excessive amount of the viewport.

Use the following values as starting points, not rigid dimensions:

- Portrait composition width: approximately 500–650px.
- Portrait composition height: approximately 580–700px.
- Content-to-image gap: approximately 80–140px.
- Main section maximum width: approximately 1440–1520px.
- Generous, responsive outer margins.

Use fluid sizing with clamp() where appropriate.

Ensure that on ultrawide monitors, the composition remains intentionally contained and does not stretch indefinitely.

The portrait and text should feel optically balanced rather than mechanically centered.

Maintain generous negative space around the image.

